    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="1103" n="1089" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1089"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Korea/2–248: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Austin</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d716-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-02T17:00:00-05:00">February 2, 1948—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Reference Australian delegation inquiry cited daily classified summary 100
                    January 27<anchor n="2" xml:id="d716-f2"/> regarding your statement on authority
                    of Korean Commission, Department’s view is that question of whether it shall on
                    own initiative observe election in south Korea separately, or as alternative
                    consult first with Interim Committee, is one for Commission itself to resolve.
                    We should regard adoption of either alternative as normal and
                    unexceptionable.</p>
                <p>Thus we do not contend this matter should not be brought before Interim
                    Committee. If Commission is disposed proceed under existing authority question
                    need not be so handled; but if Commission desires to consult, guidance may
                    assuredly be sought of Committee.</p>
                <p>You may in your discretion and upon inquiry convey these views to other
                    delegations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d716-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d716-f1-content">
                <p>Sent as 24 to Seoul introduced by “The following message has been sent to
                    USUN:”.</p>
            </note>
